---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Faq from '../components/Faq.astro';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Who is Ryan Allen?',
    a: 'Builder who ships AI systems end to end, with AI agents as the workforce and a human gate on every merge. Editor of CoreWise Academy.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What has Ryan Allen shipped?',
    a: 'Four live systems: corewise.video (six models read in parallel, 1,800+ users), kinefractal.com (519 agent-written PRs merged through a human gate, paper trading only), truenote.org (cited answers or refusal), and willaicite.com (a deterministic GEO audit, spec to live in a day). 100% of what ships passes his review first.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do you contact Ryan Allen?',
    a: 'Through GitHub at github.com/ryanportfolio: every public repo accepts issues, and the profile links back to each live system. This section is the contact point for the whole site.',
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="Ryan Allen, AI systems builder · CoreWise Academy"
  description="Ryan Allen builds and ships AI systems end to end. Four live systems, presented as a technical drawing set: corewise.video, kinefractal.com, truenote.org, willaicite.com."
  faq={faq}
  crumbs={[{ name: 'About the editor', path: '/about/' }]}
>
  <main id="aw">
    <!-- A-000 · cover -->
    <section class="sheet hero" data-sheet="A-000">
      <div class="hero-grid">
        <div class="hero-mast">
          <p class="aw-kicker">APPROVED WORKS · DRAWING SET A · WEB EDITION</p>
          <h1 class="hero-name">Ryan Allen</h1>
          <div class="hero-rule"></div>
          <p class="hero-line">AI systems builder<br />shipping end to end</p>
          <p class="hero-links">
            <a href="https://corewise.video">corewise.video</a> ·
            <a href="https://kinefractal.com">kinefractal.com</a> ·
            <a href="https://truenote.org">truenote.org</a> ·
            <a href="https://willaicite.com">willaicite.com</a><br />
            <a class="gh" href="https://github.com/ryanportfolio">github.com/ryanportfolio</a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-fig" id="fig-hero" aria-label="Six model strands converging to one synthesis, drawn in true perspective"></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- A-001 · index + line law -->
    <section class="sheet" data-sheet="A-001" id="sec-a001">
      <ol class="idx">
        <li><a href="#sec-a100"><span class="idx-no">A-100</span><span class="idx-name">CoreWise · six-model synthesis</span><span class="idx-live"><span class="ext">corewise.video ↗</span> LIVE</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-a200"><span class="idx-no">A-200</span><span class="idx-name">KineFractal · rule-based signal engine</span><span class="idx-live"><span class="ext">kinefractal.com ↗</span> LIVE</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-a300"><span class="idx-no">A-300</span><span class="idx-name">Truenote · cited answers or refusal</span><span class="idx-live"><span class="ext">truenote.org ↗</span> LIVE</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-a400"><span class="idx-no">A-400</span><span class="idx-name">WillAICite · deterministic GEO audit</span><span class="idx-live"><span class="ext">willaicite.com ↗</span> LIVE</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-a500"><span class="idx-no">A-500</span><span class="idx-name">Method of construction</span><span class="idx-tag">METHOD</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-a600"><span class="idx-no">A-600</span><span class="idx-name">Ancillary works</span><span class="idx-tag">TOOLING</span></a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-a999"><span class="idx-no">A-999</span><span class="idx-name">How this page was drawn</span><span class="idx-tag">END OF SET</span></a></li>
      </ol>

      <h3 class="sec-head">HOLDINGS · THE TEN-SECOND VERSION</h3>
      <div class="hold">
        <div class="hold-cell"><p class="hold-big" data-count="6">6</p><p class="hold-k">MODELS IN PARALLEL · 1,800+ REGISTERED USERS · COREWISE.VIDEO</p></div>
        <div class="hold-cell"><p class="hold-big" data-count="1227">1,227</p><p class="hold-k">COMMITS · 519 MERGED PRS · PAPER TRADING ONLY</p></div>
        <div class="hold-cell"><p class="hold-big funnel">40+40→8→1</p><p class="hold-k">RETRIEVAL FUNNEL · CITED ANSWER OR EXPLICIT REFUSAL</p></div>
        <div class="hold-cell"><p class="hold-big" data-count="8">8</p><p class="hold-k">AUDIT DIMENSIONS · 0 LLM CALLS · SPEC TO LIVE IN A DAY</p></div>
      </div>

      <p class="body-block">Live systems: specified, gated, checked, and approved. The agents drafted.
        An independent agent that had not seen the work checked. After feedback I approved. Human always in
        the loop for the final step after automation is complete.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- A-100 · CoreWise -->
    <section class="sheet" data-sheet="A-100" id="sec-a100">
      <header class="sheet-head ink-vermilion">
        <div>
          <p class="sheet-no">A-100</p>
          <h2 class="sheet-title">COREWISE · SYNTHESIS CHANDELIER</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="sheet-sub">MULTI-MODEL SYNTHESIS · LIVE</p>
      </header>
      <div class="cols">
        <div class="main">
          <p class="lede">One URL goes in. Six models read it in parallel. Out comes a synthesis: where
            they agree, where they split, and what only one of them saw.</p>
          <div class="fig ink-vermilion" id="fig-chandelier" aria-label="The synthesis chandelier, six strands converging to one apex"></div>
          <p class="fig-cap"><span class="fig-no">FIG 1</span>Six model strands descend from one source, cross the
            ring, and converge to one synthesis. Outputs are weight-graded: heavy convergence, medium
            divergence, fine for what only one model saw. True perspective; stroke weight falls with depth.
            This one is live: it sways in a slow breeze on its own, and your pointer splits the
            linework into a glowing chromatic echo, traced from the side you entered.</p>
          <div class="fig-row">
            <div class="fig ink-vermilion" id="fig-disc" aria-label="108 engraved spokes, one per hundred commits"></div>
            <p class="fig-cap narrow"><span class="fig-no">FIG 2</span>108 engraved spokes, one per 100 commits:
              ~10.8k GitHub-attributed commits across ~7 months. Every ninth spoke is cut heavier, so the
              twelve groups of nine can be counted by eye. Watch it count itself in.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="rail ink-vermilion">
          <p class="rail-head">COREWISE</p>
          <a class="rail-url" href="https://corewise.video">corewise.video ↗</a>
          <div class="rail-rule"></div>
          <dl>
            <dt>STATUS</dt><dd>LIVE · VERIFIED REACHABLE</dd>
            <dt>MODELS IN PARALLEL</dt><dd>6</dd>
            <dt>REGISTERED USERS</dt><dd>1,800+</dd>
            <dt>COMMITS</dt><dd>~10.8K / ~7 MO</dd>
            <dt>PLATFORMS</dt><dd>WEB · MOBILE (EXPO) · DESKTOP (TAURI) · 2 BROWSER EXTS · MCP SERVER</dd>
            <dt>BILLING / EXPORT</dt><dd>STRIPE · NOTION / PDF / TTS</dd>
          </dl>
          <p class="rail-note">“Six models because one model alone lies confidently. Where they agree I
            trust it more. Where they split, that's usually the interesting part.”</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- A-200 · KineFractal -->
    <section class="sheet" data-sheet="A-200" id="sec-a200">
      <header class="sheet-head ink-prussian">
        <div>
          <p class="sheet-no">A-200</p>
          <h2 class="sheet-title">KINEFRACTAL · TEN-GATE CORRIDOR</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="sheet-sub">RULE-BASED SIGNAL ENGINE · LIVE · PAPER</p>
      </header>
      <div class="cols">
        <div class="main">
          <p class="lede">It buys broad-market fear and sells gradually as prices rise. One engine produces every
            backtest and the nightly public signal. Ten gates stand between signal and order, and on this
            page the last two are yours to operate.</p>
          <div class="fig ink-prussian" id="fig-corridor" aria-label="Ten pre-trade gates in one-point perspective"></div>
          <div class="gate-panel">
            <p class="gate-readout" id="gate-readout">GATES CLOSED 00 / 10</p>
            <button class="aw-btn" id="btn-arm">APPROVE THE TRADE · CLOSE GATE 09</button>
            <div class="confirm-wrap" id="confirm-wrap">
              <input id="input-confirm" type="text" placeholder="TYPE TRANSMIT" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" aria-label="Type TRANSMIT to close gate 10" />
              <button class="aw-btn" id="btn-confirm">SEND THE ORDER · CLOSE GATE 10</button>
            </div>
            <p class="gate-note">This is the real protocol, miniaturized: no order goes out unless a human
              clicks approve on the exact trade, then types TRANSMIT to send it. Paper account only.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="gatekey">
            <p><b>01</b> DECISION FROM PREVIOUS CLOSED NYSE SESSION</p>
            <p><b>03</b> LEDGER AND BROKER QUANTITIES MUST AGREE</p>
            <p><b>05</b> BUYS CANNOT EXCEED AVAILABLE FUNDS</p>
            <p><b>07</b> STALE GATEWAY FAILS CLOSED</p>
            <p class="human"><b>09</b> A HUMAN APPROVES THE TRADE</p>
            <p class="human"><b>10</b> A HUMAN TYPES TRANSMIT</p>
          </div>
          <p class="fig-cap"><span class="fig-no">FIG 1</span>Ten pre-trade gates in one-point perspective; all ten
            must close before anything transmits. Six are named in the schedule (the full list is in the
            repo README). The last two belong to a human, which is why this page makes you be one.</p>
          <div class="fig ink-prussian" id="fig-strata" aria-label="Percentile fear floors for the three live strategies"></div>
          <p class="fig-cap"><span class="fig-no">FIG 2</span>The three live strategies in section: each buys only when
            its fear reading (Williams VIX Fix vs its own history) rises past the floor.</p>
          <div class="fig ink-prussian" id="fig-ledger" aria-label="69 dated ledger entries"></div>
          <p class="fig-cap"><span class="fig-no">FIG 3</span>69 dated entries in a 219 KB experiment ledger. Kills
            logged beside wins, and they stay in the book.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="rail ink-prussian">
          <p class="rail-head">KINEFRACTAL</p>
          <a class="rail-url" href="https://kinefractal.com">kinefractal.com ↗</a>
          <div class="rail-rule"></div>
          <dl>
            <dt>STATUS</dt><dd>LIVE · NIGHTLY EOD SIGNALS</dd>
            <dt>COMMITS / PRS</dt><dd>1,227 · 519 MERGED / ~1 MO</dd>
            <dt>TESTS</dt><dd>~600 ACROSS 54 FILES</dd>
            <dt>LEDGER</dt><dd>219 KB · 69 DATED ENTRIES</dd>
            <dt>PIPELINE</dt><dd>CRON → PYTHON ENGINE → POSTGRES → PUBLIC DASHBOARD</dd>
          </dl>
          <p class="rail-boxed">IBKR PAPER ACCOUNT ONLY. NOT REAL-MONEY TRADING. BACKTESTS ARE HYPOTHETICAL.</p>
          <p class="rail-note">The point is the discipline, not a returns pitch. Nothing transmits unless
            I arm it by hand.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- A-300 · Truenote -->
    <section class="sheet" data-sheet="A-300" id="sec-a300">
      <header class="sheet-head ink-viridian">
        <div>
          <p class="sheet-no">A-300</p>
          <h2 class="sheet-title">TRUENOTE · MANY SEARCHES, ONE ANSWER</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="sheet-sub">SOURCE-GROUNDED AI FOR LIVE CALLS · LIVE · PUBLIC REPO</p>
      </header>
      <div class="cols">
        <div class="main">
          <p class="lede">Built for call-center reps mid-call: every answer carries a clickable citation,
            or the system refuses out loud. Never a guess. Drag the confidence down and watch it refuse.</p>
          <div class="fig ink-viridian" id="fig-confluence" aria-label="Eighty retrieval filaments narrowing to one cited answer"></div>
          <div class="conf-panel">
            <label for="conf-slider" class="conf-label">RE-RANKING CONFIDENCE</label>
            <input id="conf-slider" type="range" min="0" max="1" step="0.01" value="0.62" />
            <p class="conf-readout" id="conf-readout"></p>
          </div>
          <p class="fig-cap"><span class="fig-no">FIG 1</span>80 candidate filaments, 40 vector and 40 BM25, flow to
            the rerank portal in dimetric projection. Eight pass at double weight; one leaves as the cited
            answer. Below the 0.30 gate the answer path goes dark and REFUSES lights, because on weak
            retrieval the LLM is never called at all. The refusal branch is drawn solid: refusing is
            shipped behavior.</p>
          <div class="fig-row">
            <div class="fig ink-viridian" id="fig-tally" aria-label="43 test files tallied"></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="rail ink-viridian">
          <p class="rail-head">TRUENOTE</p>
          <a class="rail-url" href="https://truenote.org">truenote.org ↗</a>
          <div class="rail-rule"></div>
          <dl>
            <dt>STATUS</dt><dd>LIVE · VERIFIED REACHABLE</dd>
            <dt>PUBLIC REPO</dt><dd><a href="https://github.com/ryanportfolio/Truenote">github.com/ryanportfolio/Truenote</a></dd>
            <dt>RETRIEVAL</dt><dd>VECTOR 40 + BM25 40 → RERANK 8 → 1</dd>
            <dt>TEST FILES</dt><dd>43 (VITEST)</dd>
            <dt>ROLES</dt><dd>4-TIER · CUSTOMER DATA KEPT SEPARATE ON THE SERVER</dd>
            <dt>EVALUATION</dt><dd>ANSWER ACC · CITATION ACC · REFUSAL RATE · P50/P95</dd>
          </dl>
          <p class="rail-note">“A guess during a live call is worse than no answer. So refusing correctly
            counts as a score here, not an error.”</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- A-400 · WillAICite -->
    <section class="sheet" data-sheet="A-400" id="sec-a400">
      <header class="sheet-head ink-ochre">
        <div>
          <p class="sheet-no">A-400</p>
          <h2 class="sheet-title">WILLAICITE · PROOF OF DETERMINISM</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="sheet-sub">GEO AUDIT · LIVE · SPEC TO PRODUCTION IN A DAY</p>
      </header>
      <div class="cols">
        <div class="main">
          <p class="lede">SEO gets you listed. GEO gets you quoted. It scores whether AI answer engines
            can access, extract, and quote a page. The audit deliberately contains no AI, and you can
            prove it here: run it again.</p>
          <div class="fig ink-ochre" id="fig-seals" aria-label="Two identical audit seals with zero displacement between runs"></div>
          <div class="seal-panel">
            <button class="aw-btn" id="btn-run">RUN THE AUDIT AGAIN</button>
            <p class="seal-meter" id="seal-meter"></p>
          </div>
          <p class="fig-cap"><span class="fig-no">FIG 1</span>The same URL, audited twice. The seals are the same
            drawing because the score is the same number: rule-based checks, no LLM calls, identical
            input, identical output. Every press of the button re-derives the right seal from scratch and
            hashes its geometry. The hash never changes. Dimensions I to VIII: AI crawler access,
            renderability, answer-readiness, topical focus &amp; metadata, evidence density, structured
            data, freshness, entity / E-E-A-T.</p>
          <div class="fig ink-ochre" id="fig-daybar" aria-label="Timeline of one day from spec to live with 22 PR ticks"></div>
          <p class="fig-cap"><span class="fig-no">FIG 2</span>One day, drawn to scale of itself: spec in the morning,
            live the same day. Each tick is one of 22+ PRs merged through claude/* branches, all through
            the human merge gate.</p>
          <div class="fig ink-ochre" id="fig-rings" aria-label="Three concentric SSRF guards around the hosted fetcher"></div>
          <p class="fig-cap"><span class="fig-no">FIG 3</span>The hosted fetcher inside its three guards. Plus
            politeness: robots.txt respected, a ten-fetch cap, "could not verify" over guessing.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="rail ink-ochre">
          <p class="rail-head">WILLAICITE</p>
          <a class="rail-url" href="https://willaicite.com">willaicite.com ↗</a>
          <div class="rail-rule"></div>
          <dl>
            <dt>STATUS</dt><dd>LIVE · VERIFIED REACHABLE</dd>
            <dt>SCORED DIMENSIONS</dt><dd>8</dd>
            <dt>LLM CALLS IN AUDIT PATH</dt><dd>0 · DETERMINISTIC BY DESIGN</dd>
            <dt>SPEC → LIVE</dt><dd>SAME DAY · 22+ PRS MERGED</dd>
            <dt>FETCHER</dt><dd>BLOCKED FROM REACHING INTERNAL ADDRESSES · RATE-LIMITED</dd>
          </dl>
          <p class="rail-note">And no, the audit isn't "AI-powered." It's deterministic on purpose.
            That's the whole point of a score you can trust.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- A-500 · Method -->
    <section class="sheet" data-sheet="A-500" id="sec-a500">
      <header class="sheet-head">
        <div>
          <p class="sheet-no">A-500</p>
          <h2 class="sheet-title">METHOD OF CONSTRUCTION</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="sheet-sub">HOW EVERY SHEET IN THIS SET GOT BUILT</p>
      </header>
      <div class="cols">
        <div class="main">
          <p class="lede">I ship with AI agents as the workforce. And a builder never grades its own work.</p>
          <div class="fig" id="fig-stemma" aria-label="The sixteen-agent design workflow drawn as a family tree"></div>
          <p class="fig-cap"><span class="fig-no">FIG 1</span>The 16-agent design workflow that chose
            kinefractal.com's production architecture, every agent numbered: five code readers and four
            web researchers feed three independent proposals; a three-lens judge panel scores them; one
            agent synthesizes. Then the claims were re-verified by hand (the node in the human accent)
            before production.</p>
        </div>
        <aside class="rail">
          <p class="rail-head">THE METHOD</p>
          <div class="rail-rule"></div>
          <dl>
            <dt>WORKFORCE</dt><dd>AI AGENTS</dd>
            <dt>REVIEW</dt><dd>INDEPENDENT AGENT, FRESH CONTEXT</dd>
            <dt>MERGE</dt><dd>HUMAN GATE · ALWAYS</dd>
            <dt>PROCESS</dt><dd>CAN'T-DO → CAN-DO → CHEAPER AND FASTER → IMPROVE THE SETUP → AUDIT THE OUTPUT → PRUNE WHAT DOESN'T HOLD UP → JUDGE RESULTS AND STUDY LOGS</dd>
          </dl>
          <p class="rail-note">“I don't just generate code and hope: PRs get reviewed by independent AI agents with
            fresh context.”</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- A-600 · Ancillary works -->
    <section class="sheet" data-sheet="A-600" id="sec-a600">
      <header class="sheet-head">
        <div>
          <p class="sheet-no">A-600</p>
          <h2 class="sheet-title">ANCILLARY WORKS · TOOLING &amp; WORKS IN PROGRESS</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="sheet-sub">THE SHOP THAT BUILDS THE SHIPS</p>
      </header>
      <div class="cols">
        <div class="main">
          <div class="fig-row">
            <div>
              <div class="fig" id="fig-skills" aria-label="34 skill cells, one per skill"></div>
              <p class="fig-cap narrow"><span class="fig-no">FIG 1</span><span id="skill-count">0</span> cells, one
                per skill, counted from the repo tree.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="side-copy">
              <h3 class="sec-head">AI-FIRMWARE</h3>
              <p class="body-block small">A self-syncing template: an always-loaded kernel of rules, 34
                on-demand skills, committed memory, and automatic checks that catch when it goes off track. One rule set
                for both agent tools. Versioned plugin, v1.1.1.</p>
              <p class="mono-link"><a href="https://github.com/ryanportfolio/AI-Firmware">github.com/ryanportfolio/AI-Firmware ↗</a></p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <h3 class="sec-head">LOCAL-CPU-ONLY-PTT</h3>
          <div class="fig" id="fig-ptt" aria-label="Offline dictation pipeline inside a boundary box"></div>
          <p class="fig-cap"><span class="fig-no">FIG 2</span>Offline push-to-talk dictation for Windows:
            microphone, voice activity detection, Whisper on CPU only, clipboard. The boundary box is the
            feature: no cloud, no network path, nothing leaves the machine.
            <a href="https://github.com/ryanportfolio/Local-CPU-only-PTT">Public repo ↗</a></p>
          <h3 class="sec-head">GITHELP</h3>
          <div class="fig" id="fig-githelp" aria-label="Discussion-scouting pipeline with a normally-open human switch"></div>
          <div class="go-panel"><button class="aw-btn" id="btn-go">GIVE THE HUMAN GO</button></div>
          <p class="fig-cap"><span class="fig-no">FIG 3</span>A workspace that scouts GitHub Discussions, ranks
            what's answerable, reads the full thread, and drafts a verified answer. Each answer posts to
            GitHub only after a human clicks go; one click approves one answer. The button below is that
            switch, demo-only: it closes the drawn circuit and posts nothing.</p>
          <div class="fig-row">
            <div class="fig" id="fig-pixelswarm" aria-label="Maimcoil drawn entirely in phantom line"></div>
            <div class="side-copy">
              <h3 class="sec-head">MAIMCOIL</h3>
              <p class="fig-cap"><span class="fig-no">FIG 4</span>A survivors-style action game headed for Steam:
                Tauri 2 + React with a Rust/Steamworks bridge, ~37k lines of game code. Not yet released,
                so it is drawn entirely in phantom line, per the conventions on A-001; a playable prototype
                is live at <a href="https://corewise.video/play">corewise.video/play ↗</a>. The swarm
                drifts anyway.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <aside class="rail">
          <p class="rail-head">ANCILLARY</p>
          <div class="rail-rule"></div>
          <dl>
            <dt>AI-FIRMWARE</dt><dd>PUBLIC · PLUGIN v1.1.1 · 34 SKILLS</dd>
            <dt>LOCAL-CPU-ONLY-PTT</dt><dd>PUBLIC · OFFLINE · CPU-ONLY WHISPER · <a href="https://github.com/ryanportfolio/Local-CPU-only-PTT">REPO ↗</a></dd>
            <dt>GITHELP</dt><dd>PRIVATE · HUMAN-GO GATE</dd>
            <dt>MAIMCOIL</dt><dd>STEAM GAME · PROTOTYPE · <a href="https://corewise.video/play">PLAY ↗</a></dd>
          </dl>
          <p class="rail-note">None of these are products. They're the tooling that makes the products
            shippable.</p>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- A-999 · How this page was drawn -->
    <section class="sheet last" data-sheet="A-999" id="sec-a999">
      <header class="sheet-head">
        <div>
          <p class="sheet-no">A-999</p>
          <h2 class="sheet-title">HOW THIS PAGE WAS DRAWN</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="sheet-sub">END OF SET</p>
      </header>
      <div class="cols">
        <div class="main">
          <p class="body-block">This page was built the same way the systems on it were built. A locked
            fact sheet first: every number traced to a verified catalogue before a single line was drawn.
            Then three competing art directions from independent AI agents, scored by a three-lens judge
            panel (a recruiter's eye, a book designer's eye, and one agent whose only job was hunting
            AI-generated design tells). Then the build, then the review passes.</p>
          <p class="body-block">Every figure is computed geometry: real 3D to 2D projection math running
            in your browser, emitted as vectors. The chandelier is a true perspective camera you steer.
            The corridor is one-point perspective with the human gates wired to your hand. The confluence
            is <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axonometric_projection" rel="noopener">angled 3D view</a> with a live confidence gate. Where a count is drawn, the count is the
            fact. There is also a <a href="https://github.com/ryanportfolio">print edition</a>: a 9-sheet
            vector PDF of this same set, built by the same locked facts and audited by a script that
            recounts every drawn mark.</p>
          <h3 class="sec-head">REVISIONS</h3>
          <table class="rev">
            <thead><tr><th>REV</th><th>DESCRIPTION</th><th>DATE</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>△1</td><td>DRAFTED · AI AGENTS, THREE COMPETING DIRECTIONS</td><td>2026-07-17</td></tr>
              <tr><td>△2</td><td>CHECKED · INDEPENDENT AGENTS, FRESH CONTEXT</td><td>2026-07-17</td></tr>
              <tr><td>△3</td><td>REVISED · EVERY COUNT RE-AUDITED AGAINST SOURCE</td><td>2026-07-17</td></tr>
